ling wine. Brandy generally contains 35–60% alcohol by volume and is typically consumed as an after-dinner digestif. Some brandies are aged in wooden casks. Others are coloured with caramel colouring to imitate the effect of ageing, and some are produced using a combination of ageing and colouring. Varieties of wine brandy can be found across the winemaking world. Among the most renowned are Cognac and Armagnac from southwestern France."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-brandy"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brandy"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Lobster Thermidor","dish/lobster-thermidor"]]],["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine",[["Boerenjongens","dish/boerenjongens"]]],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Lobster Thermidor","dish/lobster-thermidor"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Lobster Thermidor","dish/lobster-thermidor"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Lobster meat","ingredient/lobster-meat"],["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Sherry","ingredient/sherry"]]}]},"dish/carnation-cafe":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/carnation-cafe","n":"Carnation Cafe","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Carnation Cafe is an American comfort food restaurant located in Main Street, U.S.A. at Disneyland in Anaheim, California in the United States. The restaurant opened in 1955 as Carnation Cafe Ice Cream Parlor."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-carnation-cafe"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnation_Cafe"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["5-8 Club","dish/5-8-club"],["Alta