Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The Greenland shark (Somniosus microcephalus), also known as the grey shark or gurry shark, is a large shark of the family Somniosidae (\"sleeper sharks\"), closely related to the Pacific and southern sleeper sharks. Inhabiting the North Atlantic and Arctic Oceans, they are notable for their exceptional longevity, although they are poorly studied because of the depth and remoteness of their natural habitat."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-greenland-shark"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenland_shark"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Icelandic cuisine","cuisine/icelandic-cuisine",[["Hákarl","dish/hakarl"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Shark meat","ingredient/shark-meat"]]}]},"dish/italian-beef":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/italian-beef","n":"Italian beef","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian-American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["An Italian beef is a sandwich of Chicago origin made from thin slices of roast beef simmered and served with a thin gravy on French bread. Common toppings are a choice between spicy giardiniera (called \"hot\") or mild bell peppers (called \"sweet\"). The entire sandwich may be dipped in the juice the meat is cooked in before serving with a side of French fries."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-italian-beef"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_beef"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian-American cuisine","cuisine/italian-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Au jus","ingredient/au-jus"],["Baguette","ingredient/baguette"],["Bread roll","ingredient/bread-roll"],["Giardiniera","ingredient/giardiniera"],["Roast beef","ingredient/roast-beef"]]},{"h":"More from Italian-American cuisine","links":[["Buona","dish/buona"],["Chicken Francese","d